  "$comment": "Cross-client test vectors for src/core/rules/tide/height.ts. ADR 003 \u00a74. TWO KINDS OF AUTHORITY. (1) The samples are REAL published NOAA CO-OPS predictions for station 9410580 (Newport Bay Entrance, MLLW, metric) - at a sample instant the expected height IS the published number, so `heightAt` there is checked against NOAA, not against us. (2) Between samples the expected values were derived from Fritsch & Carlson, 'Monotone Piecewise Cubic Interpolation', SIAM J. Numer. Anal. 17(2) 1980 - the monotonicity-preserving tangent construction under the |(alpha,beta)| <= 3 constraint - reimplemented independently and evaluated with the standard cubic Hermite basis. None of these numbers came from running the TypeScript they police. `boundedBy` restates Fritsch-Carlson's own guarantee: the interpolant never leaves the range of the two samples bracketing it, which is the property that stops a curve inventing a water level NOAA never predicted.",
